Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 14:14:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08022/11362] Close 5 guard bypasses; the interlock's shared
 state and a stale procedure

Three concerns from the Layer-2 audit extension, plus the review findings on
the fixes themselves. What is CLOSED and what remains OPEN is stated per item
below -- this is not a completeness claim.

CLOSED -- determination_preservation_lint.py (the guard protecting the record):
 * DELETION and RENAME bypassed it entirely (--diff-filter=M). Deleting a
   flagged artifact is a strictly worse never-prune violation than editing one
   and was invisible. Now MDRT, matched on the OLD path so git pairs a
   cross-directory move as a rename -- the documented legacy/fabricated
   retirement path (bed0635b6) still passes.
 * FAIL-OPEN on git error: an empty file list read as "nothing changed". Every
   error path now refuses. One carve-out (a path genuinely absent at a rev)
   is stderr-matched, including git's index-absent spelling, which does NOT
   contain "does not exist in".
 * A PRINCIPLE-WRAPPED determination lifted a quarantine silently: raw
   `is True` never matches {"principle":..,"value":true}, which CLAUDE.md
   permits for ANY field. This was QA-Layer origin bug #2 reproduced inside
   the guard whose own docstring cites it. All 4 sites unwrapped.
 * EMPTYING a protected field in place bypassed every rule (name-only checks;
   rule 4 treats an unrankable value as "not a downgrade"). Calibrated over
   400 commits / 1,804 artifact-pairs: deleted 130x, emptied 0x -- zero
   false-positive cost.
 * The _cleared_deliberately exemption was trivially satisfiable: any key
   pairing "cleared" with "note" excused any determination, and cache_cleared
   is a real key shape here. The note must now name the field it excuses.
Also: the hook never ran on deletion-only commits (pre-commit's own file list
excludes D) -- always_run landed earlier in abc6a823c; this commit supplies
the other half, so HEAD is no longer wiring-without-fix.

CLOSED -- test_suite_mutation_check.py concurrency:
 Per-run baselines replace the single shared snapshot (chose immutable
 per-run files over a lock; HEAD-comparison was rejected on evidence --
 excluding already-dirty work IS the mechanism, and this tree carried 84
 dirty files). Race 1, the severe one and not in the brief, is closed: a
 passing run used to unlink the marker unconditionally, so a clean run
 disarmed the interlock while another run's rewrite sat on disk. Markers now
 retire on tree evidence, not ownership -- concurrent agent workflows share
 a PPID, so ownership keys do not work here. --restore's backup is preserved.

CLOSED -- a procedure the fix had invalidated:
 --check now REFUSES without a baseline, but CLAUDE.md still told the operator
 to run it bare (and its STOP paragraph still described the deleted shared
 snapshot; known-issues still called it "the only backstop"). conftest's
 runtime warning pointed there too, though its baseline is in-memory so
 --check could only refuse. All four updated to --gate / a paired baseline,
 verified end-to-end rather than asserted.

OPEN -- deliberately not closed here:
 * verifier_authenticity_lint.py is in scope and AUDITED, and the audit's
   finding is confirmed and NOT fixed: a verifier claiming NTK+SAE with no
   torch, fabricating data via `activations = np.random.randn`, capping with
   min(x, 0.999) and padding duration_s scores ZERO violations -- it is both
   exemplars CLAUDE.md names and it passes. Widening is a false-positive call
   reserved to the operator; the audit never edits.
 * pages_fever_dream_lint.py stays acknowledged out of scope, re-decided on
   evidence (read + audited, SILENT_NON_FIRING, every miss is presentation
   bloat, none gates a claim). Nothing re-examines it on a cadence; the
   forcing function for that was deliberately NOT shipped while a bulk
   migration is live in this tree.
 * Marker cross-attribution is unfixed by design: a tree-wide diff cannot
   tell whose write it was. Fail-closed (over-report, never miss).
 * The 110 skipped tests remain unaudited against "Tests Must Run and Assert".

Verification: 162 tests pass on the changed surface; mutation testing killed
9/10 mutants (M10 reported unkillable and left honestly untested rather than
covered by a test that only appears to); both hook entrypoints green; --all
sweep of 15,331 artifacts flags nothing. One test expectation was deliberately
REVERSED and documented in place (an unparseable new side was treated as never
a violation, so `> file` scored clean); nothing was weakened to pass.

Staged explicitly, not with -A: 4 cron-watcher files were dirty before this
session and are left alone -- an -A sweep is how this workflow's own earlier
change ended up in another's commit.

